#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c364b9-d7be-545b-8bb2-ae86c4c7fcd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40c364b9-d7be-545b-8bb2-ae86c4c7fcd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534389} :answer-field/id #uuid "9908f8c2-74fa-5229-9b2a-2eddd163b590" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534917} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5315806-a439-585f-85b6-8fe87007f878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5315806-a439-585f-85b6-8fe87007f878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534671} :answer-field/id #uuid "f62681d9-cd8d-595e-ba4f-a4722ad371ab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534966} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb24c4f0-6957-5fc0-b36b-ba0d18bb9054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb24c4f0-6957-5fc0-b36b-ba0d18bb9054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534789} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb5a8c81-2643-51d7-9805-3937d851aee1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534968}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d2f4bec-f2bc-5622-80f4-e5a5ebaa94bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-321990" :question/problem "The Cartesian equation of the circle defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi \n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$(x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)^{2}+(y\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$)^{2}=$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2 & =\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{6}{5}(x+2) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{36}{25}(x+2)^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+3 & =\\frac{5}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{6}{5}(y+3) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{36}{25}{(y+3)}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{36}{25}(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{36}{25}{(y+3)}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{36}{25}(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{36}{25}{(y+3)}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+{(y+3)}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation is ${(x+2)}^{2}+{(y+3)}^{2}=\\frac{25}{36}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535004 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31a45883-2a84-5b7d-9f25-dbf675d5147b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=32\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=32\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534362} {:answer/id #uuid "47bf6ae0-f1fd-5c54-9d5a-c1dcfb3a7ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534402} {:answer/id #uuid "b1144781-3992-58e7-b541-3766be87a4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534660} {:answer/id #uuid "c2332f56-6db7-5b68-8801-e4c7db637aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534700} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b32d97-9055-5b1f-81e6-1ec5f053894d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2332f56-6db7-5b68-8801-e4c7db637aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534700} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd164691-a7a0-5f7f-b4dc-78db7c18f818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41e7831f-c290-5b73-a0b9-fe7067c749d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-15857" :question/problem "![](images/33/33070b4b871552c4c45f21f0885cbce45ff65eb278cb000e68c91adfc2ab004c.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $16$ centered at the origin, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(16,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$ centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0).$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=16.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26128e9c-9d9e-57af-b197-f06d328fb1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534346} {:answer/id #uuid "4760e9b3-e753-55b3-8549-49c79fed671e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534399} {:answer/id #uuid "49a18dee-f7bf-5c98-846a-ecb30433c784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534407} {:answer/id #uuid "b09c9317-b0eb-5d82-b83b-452a31eca1a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534658} {:answer/id #uuid "e11feadc-e5a5-59e9-aa5a-84838827e52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4760e9b3-e753-55b3-8549-49c79fed671e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534399} :answer-field/id #uuid "091e02c8-01f9-5997-be0f-efbf60f36431" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58130b5b-5f37-553e-8991-9f3dd2a84005" :question/math-academy-id "q-106297" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {x}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\frac{1}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1312b130-f076-56dc-a6ca-175281e64d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534305} {:answer/id #uuid "3090c984-5ed8-5035-ba5b-4c5acd082c78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534360} {:answer/id #uuid "477bc9a6-005d-535c-b4ab-779587a92597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534401} {:answer/id #uuid "644dced5-34e6-5f21-8852-dbfa2b44f065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534466} {:answer/id #uuid "9f759471-c9f9-5e4b-a90e-babe10376f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "644dced5-34e6-5f21-8852-dbfa2b44f065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534466} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c98d58f-3fec-5e1a-83a6-98106a7cf5a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5bcab4b1-53e9-547b-81a4-3bf0881c104a" :question/math-academy-id "q-6891" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {x}^{2} & =(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {y}^{2} & =(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =16{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =16{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +16{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =16({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =16(1) \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7988efe9-2597-5390-9e57-33004a453a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7988efe9-2597-5390-9e57-33004a453a49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534524} :answer-field/id #uuid "20006ed3-e230-529e-81fb-8b1bee54d924" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98a5631a-e7cc-5569-afb2-d11edaf4836d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98a5631a-e7cc-5569-afb2-d11edaf4836d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534606} :answer-field/id #uuid "7156cc32-810c-50dc-a3b4-4e2b4679767b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e3d47e1-6723-5134-bd1d-2937862c014c" :question/math-academy-id "q-321957" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca3a73d411d7b766196a2bebf56f9d678aba54a4f2265ac08c36d0fb3fbf03b0.png)\n\nThe arc of the circle above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$ Assume $\\theta $ is between $0$ and $2\\pi .$\n\n$\\theta \\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=6.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to the arc above, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/37/37665aa7ea5388a1162ca68a1662aaa86d6369f083d7563dbf27c521c13a7c72.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]$, we get the required arc of the circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the arc of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bd82803-6b71-55a2-8f5a-355333a844cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd82803-6b71-55a2-8f5a-355333a844cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534449} :answer-field/id #uuid "03df2f8e-3e63-5aea-98dc-2a4a0017437a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534830} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ace4a688-90ad-5fc0-a3eb-fc362a726947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/val